 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to authorizing the\ncreation of \"Survivors of the Shield\" license plates",
    "basePrintNo": "S3426",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3426-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §404-ff, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3426\n\nSPONSOR: MARTINEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in\nrelation to authorizing the creation of \"Survivors of the Shield\"\nlicense plates\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill statutorily establishes the Survivor of the Shield specialized\nlicense plate, to honor fallen police officers and waives the additional\nrenewal fee on these license plates for the parents, spouse or children\nof these fallen officers.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the Vehicle and Traffic Law by creating a new section\n404-ee, which establishes in statute, the Survivor of the Shield License\nPlate and specifies that the parents, children and spouse of a fallen\nofficer should not be charged any additional renewal fees for this\nspecialized license plate.\n\nSection 2 provides that this act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew York State DMV currently issues specialized license plates to fami-\nlies of fallen police officers. The Not-for-Profit, Survivors of the\nShield, currently accepts applications for these specialized license\nplates and upon approval from the organization, and payment of a fee,\nDMV issues these specialized plates.\n\nThis bill would waive the additional bi-annual renewal fee for these\nspecialized license plates when the individual acquiring the license\nplate is the parent, spouse or child of the fallen officer. This bill\nretains the additional application fee for these specialized license\nplates, and would still require the payment of the normal renewal fee.\nThe only fee being waived through this legislation is that additional\nrenewal assessment that is placed on specialized license plates that\nhave already been paid for by the applicant through their initial regis-\ntration fee.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nMinimal.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
